        };
    ;
opRun();

THE ODOMETER'S POPULATION, GENERATED AT RUN TIME AND NEVER READ FROM A FILE.

This is incant/fixits/countInputInTmp's lesson applied at birth. The scaffold
count reads its rule list from /tmp/b2/rules.txt, a file that does not survive a
reboot and whose absence produces a SHORTER run with identical wording rather
than an error. This file exists so the odometer can never have that defect: the
list is recomputed from the live registry on every run.

The four filters are the harness's own, matching incant/f31's fbWalk exactly --
not noPrint, not a bin, is a rule, actionType zero.

⚠ THE CURSOR `opCur` IS DELIBERATELY NOT DECLARED IN THE define BLOCK. Bear-trap
38: a cursor named there limits the walk to exactly one member, silently, at
exit 0. The first draft of countInputInTmp reported 1 and looked healthy. Do not
"tidy" this by declaring it.
